#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0342 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "THE group= DISCRIMINATOR. ESCALATE on mismatch. Two rows with DIFFERENT STUDYIDs, each declaring SDESIGN once: evalRecordCountGrouped buckets by STUDYID so each group counts 1 and neither row fires. If the group list were ignored the whole-table count would be 2 and BOTH rows would fire, so honouring and ignoring it give opposite verdicts here. Two STUDYIDs in one TS is not realistic submission data; it is deliberate. The same group list is now also the Grouping block's variable (M3-D17), so this fixture pins both."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset TS label="Trial Summary" class="TRIAL DESIGN"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | SDESIGN | Study Design | PARALLEL
S2 | TS | 1 | SDESIGN | Study Design | PARALLEL
---
